From: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Subject: KVM: s390: pci: Fix handling of AIF enable without AISB
Patch-mainline: v7.2-rc4
Git-commit: 3e3aa6da87d30a0064a17b836685cd43c90a3572
References: bsc#1277451

Description: KVM/s390/pci: Fix resource leaks and cleanup in error paths
Symptom: resource leaks, denial-of-service
Problem: Error paths in interrupt forwarding logic for passthrough PCI devices
         failed to cleanup resources correctly.       
Solution: Fix the logic and handle cleanup appropriately.      
Reproduction:  -

Upstream-Description:

              KVM: s390: pci: Fix handling of AIF enable without AISB

              When a guest seeks to register IRQs without a summary bit specified,
              ensure that the associated GAITE then stores 0 for the guest AISB
              location instead of virt_to_phys(page_address(NULL)).

              Fixes: 3c5a1b6f0a18 ("KVM: s390: pci: provide routines for enabling/disabling interrupt forwarding")
              Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
              Reviewed-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
              Signed-off-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
              Signed-off-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>


Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Acked-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
---
 arch/s390/kvm/pci.c |   11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
@@ -302,9 +302,14 @@ static int kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable(struc
 
 	gaite->gisc = fib->fmt0.isc;
 	gaite->count++;
-	gaite->aisbo = fib->fmt0.aisbo;
-	gaite->aisb = virt_to_phys(page_address(aisb_page) + (fib->fmt0.aisb &
-							      ~PAGE_MASK));
+	if (fib->fmt0.sum == 1) {
+		gaite->aisbo = fib->fmt0.aisbo;
+		gaite->aisb = virt_to_phys(page_address(aisb_page) +
+					   (fib->fmt0.aisb & ~PAGE_MASK));
+	} else {
+		gaite->aisbo = 0;
+		gaite->aisb = 0;
+	}
 	aift->kzdev[zdev->aisb] = zdev->kzdev;
 	spin_unlock_irq(&aift->gait_lock);
 
